  <p class="post--date">20 Mar 2023 (Last Modified 22 Apr 2026)</p><br>
    
  <p><h2>My Reading List</h2></p>
   My list of books I've read, with marginalia.

**2025** I started noting books that I started and didn't finish.








### Books That I Remember When I Read Them

 
<li> [Katabasis](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/210191773-katabasis) by R. F. Kuang  _(Finished 1 August 2026)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [First Principles: What America's Founders Learned from the Greeks and Romans and How That Shaped Our Country]() by Thomas E. Ricks  _(Finished 25 July 2026)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Wild Dark Shore](https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D12WJTBYrw) by Charlotte McConaghy  _(Finished 20 July 2026)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Health and Safety](https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CQJK4FR1) by   _(Finished 10 July 2026)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Under the Eye of the Big Bird](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/205673377-under-the-eye-of-the-big-bird?) by Hiromi Kawakami  _(Stopped 25 March 2026)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>Perhaps it was the translation, but I found the narrative superficial barely describing the characters.


</li>
 
<li> [The Children of Jocasta](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/33667103-the-children-of-jocasta) by Natalie Haynes  _(Finished 20 March 2026)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>Great book. Not as familiar with the Theban cycle as the Trojan one.


</li>
 
<li> [Otherworldly](https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F2SFWM92) by Dwain Worrell  _(Finished 14 March 2026)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [What Writers Read](https://nypl.overdrive.com/media/9043370) by Pandora Sykes  _(Finished 5 February 2026)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Empire of AI](https://nypl.overdrive.com/media/11435637) by Karen Hao  _(Finished 31 January 2026)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [The Denial of Death](https://www.amazon.com/Denial-Death-Ernest-Becker-ebook/dp/B002C7Z57C) by Ernest Becker  _(Finished 30 January 2026)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Under the Eye of the Big Bird: A Novel](https://www.amazon.com/Under-Eye-Big-Bird-Novel-ebook/dp/B0CPDSX2C1/) by Hiromi Kawakami  _(Finished 25 January 2026)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [The Creative Act](https://nypl.overdrive.com/media/9040747) by Rick Rubin  _(Finished 22 January 2026)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>I didn't get much from this book, which I listened to as an audiobook, other than the idea that creativity is a process and go with the flow.


</li>
 
<li> [The Consolations of Philosophy](https://www.amazon.com/Consolations-Philosophy-Vintage-International-ebook/dp/B00ATLA8RU/) by Alain de Botton  _(Finished 20 January 2026)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>I didn't get much  out of his descriptions of the philosophers and think his portrayal of Montaigne was inaccurate. The idea is good, the execution is poor.


</li>
 
<li> [There is No Place for Us, Working and Homeless in America](https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0CW8MF8VV) by Brian Goldstone  _(Finished 14 January 2026)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Wisdom Takes Work](https://www.amazon.com/Wisdom-Takes-Work-Repeat-Virtues/dp/0593191730) by Ryan Holiday  _(Finished 8 January 2026)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>This book would provide insight into how some people achieved greatness, but, after the introduuction, there is little unity in exposition other than a rambling and repetitive tone. 


</li>
 
<li> [Something To Do With Paying Attention](https://www.mcnallyjackson.com/book/9781946022271) by David Foster Wallace  _(Finished 10 December 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>This novella got me back into DFW. I first read it in the Pale King, but didn't appreciate its message about how critical moments can give perspective.


</li>
 
<li> [The Burning God](https://www.amazon.com/Burning-God-Novel-R-Kuang/dp/B084VP8KNB) by R.F. Kuang  _(Finished 20 November 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [The Dragon Republic](https://www.amazon.com/Dragon-Republic-Novel-R-Kuang/dp/0062662589) by R.F. Kuang  _(Finished 17 November 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [The Poppy War](https://www.amazon.com/Poppy-War-Novel-R-Kuang/dp/0062662562) by R.F. Kuang  _(Finished 15 November 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Exploding the Phone](https://www.amazon.com/Exploding-Phone-Phil-Lapsley/dp/0802122280/) by Hil Lapsley  _(Finished 12 November 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Friends with words : adventures in languageland]() by Martha Barnette  _(Stopped 9 November 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>Rambling, little novel. I found the style too kitcshy.


</li>
 
<li> [Beyond the Little Blue Box](https://www.amazon.com/Beyond-Little-Blue-Box-Biographical-ebook/dp/B0CQ94TKY3) by John Draper  _(Stopped 6 November 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>The book was poorly written and meandered. I had already read Exploding the Phone. This didn't add more, or at least by 50 pages in, it wasn't clear it was going to.


</li>
 
<li> [Language City](https://www.amazon.com/Language-City-Preserve-Endangered-Tongues/dp/0802164196/) by Ross Perlin  _(Stopped 5 November 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Mindmasters: the data-driven science of predicting and changing human behavior](https://www.amazon.com/Mindmasters-Data-Driven-Predicting-Changing-Behavior/dp/1647826314) by Sandra Matz  _(Stopped 4 November 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>Afterf 100 pages the book contained nothing novel and too many extended personal anecdotes.


</li>
 
<li> [The Hearing Trupmet](https://www.amazon.com/Hearing-Trumpet-Leonora-Carrington/dp/1681374641) by   _(Stopped 20 October 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>I found this book rambling and not in a good DFW or Jose Saramago way.


</li>
 
<li> [What in me is dark: the revolutionary afterlife of Paradise Lost](https://www.amazon.com/What-Me-Dark-Revolutionary-Afterlife/dp/1662602790) by Orlando Reade  _(Finished 11 September 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Unworthy]() by Agustina Bazterrica  _(Finished 8 July 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>This was a great and lyrical read. I think I will read it in Spanish. I imagine there is subtext I missed on a first read and in translation.


</li>
 
<li> [The Mountain in the Sea](https://us.macmillan.com/books/9780374605957/themountaininthesea/) by Ray Nayler  _(Stopped 20 May 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>The writing was slow, the characters banal. It seems I'm not the only one who didn't find the book engagaing (<a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/books/comments/17qvu00/am_i_missing_something_the_mountain_in_the_sea/'>Reddit</a>).


</li>
 
<li> [Free Day](https://www.nyrb.com/products/free-day) by Inès Cagnati  _(Stopped 10 May 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>The book started out bleak and unoriginal. A beleagured protagonist, out-of-place, abused by her family and ostracized by her peers. Perhaps it is more lyrical in French.


</li>
 
<li> [The Witch of Colchis](https://www.amazon.com/Witch-Colchis-Rosie-Helwett/dp/1914519080) by Rosie Helwett  _(Finished 15 April 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Nouvelle Babel](https://www.amazon.com/Nouvelle-Babel-Michel-Bussi/dp/226630679X) by Michel Bussi  _(Finished 10 April 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [The Golem and the Jinn](https://www.amazon.com/Golem-Jinn-Helene-Wecker/dp/0062110844) by Helene Wecker  _(Finished 1 April 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Andromeda: A Space Age Tale](https://www.amazon.com/Andromeda-Space-Age-Tale-Yefremov/dp/1497377730) by Ivan Yefremov  _(Finished 25 February 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Forty Days and Forty Nights](https://www.amazon.com/Forty-Days-Nights-Justin-Scott/dp/0593653960) by Amber Edwards and Justin Scott  _(Finished 20 February 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Dracula](https://www.amazon.com/Dracula-Penguin-Classics-Bram-Stoker-ebook/dp/B005JZ9PAC/) by Bram Stoker  _(Finished 10 February 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [A Spartan's Sorrow](https://www.amazon.com/Spartans-Sorrow-ancient-Greeces-formidable-ebook/dp/B08GHT36WL) by Hannah Lynn  _(Finished 2 February 2025)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [The Year of Reading Dangerously: How Fifty Great Books (and Two Not-So-Great Ones) Saved My Life](https://www.amazon.com/Year-Reading-Dangerously-Fifty-Not-So-Great-ebook/dp/B00IHZM2RY) by Andy Miller  _(Stopped 25 January 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>This book was a rambling memoir. Not a good discussion of the books or juxtaposition of their themes with modern life.


</li>
 
<li> [Andromeda](https://www.amazon.com/Andromeda-Nebula-Ivan-Yefremov/dp/1497377730/) by Ivan Yefremov  _(Finished 21 January 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>This was a fantastic book.


</li>
 
<li> [Ariadne's Crown](https://www.amazon.com/Ariadnes-Crown-Meadoe-Hora-ebook/dp/B07XVTTGB9/) by Meadoe Hora  _(Stopped 5 January 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>This book was so poorly written that I could not finish it. Just not my style. It underscored <a href='https://benjaminmcevoy.com/' target='_blank'>Ben McEvoy's</a> admonition to avoid the literary equivalent of junk food. Other writers have done better with this material.


</li>
 
<li> [Song of Sacrifice](https://www.amazon.com/Song-Sacrifice-Homeric-Chronicles-Book-ebook/dp/B07HY1FSWC) by Janell Rhiannon  _(Finished 2 January 2025)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>This book, for me, lacked substance. It explored superficially the very interesting topics of the relationships between Achilles and Oenone and Priam and Hecuba. All the males were portrayed as one-dimensional as the women in the Iliad.


</li>
 
<li> [Queens of Themyscira](https://amazon.com/Queens-Themiscyra-enthralling-fearsome-daughters-ebook/dp/B09D774V4Z) by Hannah Lynn  _(Finished 28 December 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Homer and His Iliad](https://www.amazon.com/Homer-His-Iliad-Robin-Fox/dp/0143125269) by Robin Lane Fox  _(Finished 24 December 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Orbital](https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/0802163629/) by Samantha Harvey  _(Finished 20 December 2024)_ 


<b>Notes: </b>I found the book too slow and the characters not engaging. Her writing is lyrical but, to me, it felt like it was trying too hard to be poetic.


</li>
 
<li> [Demon Copperhead](https://www.amazon.com/Demon-Copperhead-Novel-Barbara-Kingsolver/dp/0063251981) by Barbara Kingsolver  _(Finished 12 December 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [The Atlas Six](https://www.amazon.com/Atlas-Six-Olivie-Blake/dp/1250854512/) by Olivie Blake  _(Finished 14 November 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Parole de  Machines](https://www.amazon.com/Parole-machines-Alexei-Grinbaum/dp/2021441467) by Alexei Grinbaum  _(Finished 4 November 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Monstrilio](https://www.amazon.com/Monstrilio-Novel-Gerardo-S%C3%A1mano-C%C3%B3rdova/dp/1638930368) by Gerardo Sámano Córdova  _(Finished 2 November 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [In the Miso Soup](https://www.amazon.com/Miso-Soup-Ryu-Murakami/dp/014303569X) by Ryu Murakami  _(Finished 2 November 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Novelist as a Vocation](https://www.amazon.com/Novelist-Vocation-Haruki-Murakami/dp/059331817B09XM5G793) by Haruki Murakami  _(Finished 24 October 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [The Magicians](https://www.amazon.com/Magicians-Novel-Trilogy/dp/0452296293) by Lev Grossman  _(Finished 20 October 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Spies, Lies, and Algorithms](https://www.amazon.com/Spies-Lies-Algorithms-Intelligence-Information/dp/0691211917) by Amy Zegart  _(Finished 17 October 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [La Traversée des Temps (Tome 1)](https://www.frenchbooksonline.com/la-traversee-des-temps-eric-emmanuel-schmitt) by Eric-Emmanuel Schmidt  _(Finished 10 October 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Lords of Uncreation](https://www.amazon.com/Lords-Uncreation-Adrian-Tchaikovsky/dp/1781089644) by Adrian Tchaikovsky  _(Finished 10 April 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [The Portable Twentieth-Century Russian Reader](https://www.amazon.com/Portable-Twentieth-Century-Russian-Reader-Penguin/dp/0140151036) by Clarence Brown  _(Finished 8 April 2024)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Les chambres de bois](https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Les_Chambres_de_bois) by Anne Hébert  _(Finished 28 December 2023)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Lavinia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavinia_(novel)) by Ursula K. LeGuin  _(Finished 12 December 2023)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Psychonauts](https://www.amazon.com/Psychonauts-Drugs-Making-Modern-Mind/dp/0300257945/ref=sr_1_2?keywords=Psychonauts&qid=1702153597&sr=8-2) by Mike Jay  _(Finished 8 December 2023)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [The Postmortal](https://www.amazon.com/Postmortal-Drew-Magary/dp/0143119826) by Drew Magary  _(Finished 18 October 2023)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Ithaca](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/59416521-ithaca) by Claire North  _(Finished 13 October 2023)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [Ulysse from Bagdad](https://www.amazon.com/ULYSSE-BAGDAD-Schmitt/dp/2846664765) by Éric-Emmanuel Schmidt  _(Finished 4 October 2023)_ 



</li>
 
<li> [The American Canon](https://www.amazon.com/American-Canon-Literary-Emerson-Pynchon/dp/1598536400) by Harold Bloom  _(Finished 22 September 2023)_ 



</li>
 
